        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.159
          ],
          "content": "In the symbol for an LED, the triangle points to the direction in which the current can flow. The two arrows indicate that an LED emits light (Fig. 3.13b)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.16,
            0.885,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": "By using symbols to represent electrical components, it is easier to draw and understand electrical circuits. A representation of an electrical circuit using symbols is called its **circuit diagram**."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.273,
            0.529,
            0.294
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 3.10: Let us draw"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.309,
            0.882,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": " Using symbols shown in Table 3.2, **draw** the circuit diagram of an electrical circuit given in Fig. 3.12a and Fig. 3.10c."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.352,
            0.882,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "Are your circuit diagrams similar to Fig. 3.14a and Fig. 3.14b respectively?"
        },
